---
// The Method, shown by its result. The six stages live in full at
// theconvictionengine.com, so this section carries the proof instead:
// Lisa Nichols introducing Platte on stage, in her words.
---

<section id="method" class="section fade-in">
  <div class="wrap">
    <figure class="lm">
      <div class="lm-photo">
        <div class="lm-frame">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/images/lisa-platte-houston.webp" type="image/webp" />
            <img
              src="/images/lisa-platte-houston.jpg"
              alt="Lisa Nichols on stage with her hand on Platte Clark's shoulder at Speak & Write in Houston"
              width="1085" height="1355" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            />
          </picture>
        </div>
        <span class="lm-credit">Speak &amp; Write &middot; Houston &middot; 2026</span>
      </div>

      <div class="lm-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Method</span>
        <blockquote class="lm-quote">
          &ldquo;We had a writer who was good. But we needed a writer who was <span class="display-italic">phenomenal.</span>&rdquo;
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption class="lm-cite">
          Lisa Nichols
          <span>New York Times Bestselling Author &middot; Seven Books, Multiple Bestsellers<br />Featured in <em>The Secret</em> and on Oprah &middot; 88 Million People Reached</span>
        </figcaption>
        <p class="lm-method">
          Every book we build runs on the Conviction Engine&trade;: the
          stages that turn what an author knows into what a reader does.
        </p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="https://theconvictionengine.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See how the engine works ↗</a>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lm {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .lm-frame { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  .lm-frame img {
    display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 28%;
  }
  .lm-credit {
    display: block; margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.6rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-mute);
  }
  .lm-copy .eyebrow { display: block; }
  .lm-quote {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 1.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.14;
    color: var(--color-ink); text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lm-cite {
    font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .lm-cite span { display: block; margin-top: 0.35rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-ink-mute); line-height: 1.7; }
  .lm-cite em { font-style: normal; }
  .lm-method {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 1.1rem; padding-top: 1.6rem; max-width: 40ch;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  /* The photograph settles out of a slight zoom as it scrolls into view. */
  @keyframes lmSettle { from { transform: scale(1.12); } to { transform: scale(1); } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
      .lm-frame img {
        animation: lmSettle linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 0% cover 50%;
      }
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .lm { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
    .lm-frame img { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-position: 50% 22%; }
  }
</style>
